 able to control  these tumors  suggesting that there is a potential for  cartoon therapy  or specifically rms tumors  the point i didn't elaborate on in this  too much in this talk  but important to note out is that the  intra-tumor delivery of car t cells did  not provide any benefit over the  intravenous delivery  this is likely because of the stromal  regions that develop  in the tumors  it's likely that our t cells are being  um  our t cells are weaving  tumor logician itself and being  specifically brought into stromal  regions where they have little to no  effect  on the tumor growth itself  and finally we define some of the tumor  defenses defenses that we need to  overcome  and delivery of t cells induces stromal  formation in rms tumors which prevents  the infiltration of t cells into the  tumor  likely through the action of mdscs  or tumor associated macrophages in the  resulting stroma  furthermore multiple salval soluble  factors in the tme  may prevent car t function including  gigf beta mif  lif and idol 1.  so  our next steps are to first optimize the  ftfr4car to function at a lower  threshold of target molecules  and two to overcome tumor  microenvironments i think both of these  approaches are going to be necessary in  this tumor model  we are building new tools to test these  hypotheses  we now have an mif lif  gcl24 and combined mif-lif knockout cell  lines or rms which we are testing in  vivo  additionally we are also targeting pdl1  signaling by using pd1 blocking  antibodies to see if that is sufficient  in  improving the function of these fgfr4  cars  and on the card engineering side  we're developing several new cars that  have been shown  by others who have improved in vivo  function  that will target molecule densities  as shown in this cartoon in the bottom  right  in summary rms like many other solid  tubers will take a targeted approach to  overcome  we're developing optimized cars  on with cars with multiple multiple  targets  and logic gated cars  we're also targeting many of the tumor  defenses such as tgf beta signaling  we're targeting lif mif ccl 24 soluble  factors  as well as pdl1pt1 signaling  and metabolic t-cell suppression from  idol one  in addition to these  molecular  defenses  we're also targeting  we're looking at the presence of  immunosuppressive cells such as  tumor-associated macrophages  and myeloid deprived suppressor cells  we believe that this multi-targeted  approach will be  necessary  but we'll be able to overcome rms tumors  may give hope for the sound therapy  where they're most desperately  desperately needed  finally i'd like to thank the many  people who contributed to this project  well as well as the funding sources  thank you for your attention
 

